	regionKind = "dungeon",
	kind = "region",
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[Razorfen Downs is a vast warren of giant thorns at the southern edge of {link:the-barrens}The Barrens{/link}, where the plains fall away toward {link:thousand-needles}Thousand Needles{/link}. The {link:quilboar}quilboar{/link} hold it to be the most sacred of all their places. Its gate is a cave in the thorns shaped like the open jaws of a great boar. Beneath the dome of thorns lie the burial grounds of their people, and the seat of their high priests. Now the dead of the Downs do not rest. The {link:scourge}Scourge{/link} has come to {link:kalimdor}Kalimdor{/link}, and it has made the holy warren a stronghold of the dead.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[The {link:quilboar}quilboar{/link} say that the demigod Agamaggan fell in the {link:the-barrens}Barrens{/link} long ago, and that thorns grew wherever his blood touched the earth. The greatest of those thickets is the Razorfen, which they believe is his very body. The Downs and {link:razorfen-kraul}Razorfen Kraul{/link} rose from the same mighty vines. The caged mystic {link:mangletooth}Mangletooth{/link} says that the Downs are the most holy of all, because their entrance is Agamaggan's own maw, which swallows those who are not loyal to him. No chronicle records when the quilboar first made their home here.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "The Present Day",
			text = [=[A lich called {link:amnennar-the-coldbringer}Amnennar the Coldbringer{/link} rules the Downs. The high priests of the {link:quilboar}quilboar{/link}, the {link:death-s-head}Death's Head{/link}, have bound themselves to him, and many of their tribe now walk as withered undead. Skeletons march through the tunnels and a great abomination gorges itself on the dead. The quilboar drag captives here from across the {link:the-barrens}Barrens{/link}. Near the entrance stands an idol where those captives are burned and eaten.

Word has spread. A {link:scourge}Scourge{/link} envoy, {link:ambassador-malcin}Ambassador Malcin{/link}, waits outside the gate and has written to the crone who rules {link:razorfen-kraul}the Kraul{/link}. The {link:night-elves}night elf{/link} {link:myriam-moonsinger}Myriam Moonsinger{/link} watches the warren from a hill to the south. In the {link:undercity}Undercity{/link}, {link:varimathras}Varimathras{/link} has learned of the envoy, and in {link:stormwind-city}Stormwind{/link}, {link:archbishop-benedictus}Archbishop Benedictus{/link} has heard of the lich. Both want him destroyed.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Within the Downs",
			text = [=[• {b}The Gate.{/b} The boar-jawed arch opens in the thorns on the southern edge of the {link:the-barrens}Barrens{/link}. {link:death-s-head}Death's Head{/link} cultists and {link:quilboar}quilboar{/link} warriors gather around it.
• {b}The Pens.{/b} Near the entrance the quilboar keep their prisoners. Among them are a cook from {link:stormwind-city}Stormwind{/link} named {link:henry-stern}Henry Stern{/link} and a stranger who calls himself {link:belnistrasz}Belnistrasz{/link}.
• {b}The Idol.{/b} A great idol near the gate serves the quilboar as an oven for their captives.
• {b}The Chamber of the Gong.{/b} A great gong hangs in a webbed hall. Something blind and hungry waits beyond it, listening.
• {b}The Bone Pile.{/b} A dead shaman, {link:mordresh-fire-eye}Mordresh Fire Eye{/link}, dances on a mound of skulls among his skeletal brothers.
• {b}The Spiral of Thorns.{/b} A mountain of vines winds up to the summit where {link:amnennar-the-coldbringer}the Coldbringer{/link} holds his court. {link:glutton}Glutton{/link} lumbers along its lower paths.]=],
		},
	},
})

